                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fd7acff6-a6fb-3933-b6d5-81b93e03201b",
                        "entry_id": "6c3a3256-8352-30c7-953a-6c8adf0dc81a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Tending to stultify."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0cba9055-47d8-413c-a429-ba96fd8ef108",
                                "sense_id": "fd7acff6-a6fb-3933-b6d5-81b93e03201b",
                                "text": "Indeed, the government’s stultifying response betrays an attitude reminiscent of the old mission vicar: only we know what’s really good for them (see Scullion above)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ba8e9422-9bd6-4e31-ab2a-fff487350f6c",
                                "sense_id": "fd7acff6-a6fb-3933-b6d5-81b93e03201b",
                                "text": "The Judge was from an era when a person could get away with being larger than life — unlike the present day, when so much of our stultifying public discourse has come to be about joining in unearned moral superiority to look down our noses."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fa325447-e279-4e09-b6e8-416377702345",
                                "sense_id": "fd7acff6-a6fb-3933-b6d5-81b93e03201b",
                                "text": "Was it just me or did you find everyone in high school stultifying?"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
